  "body": "Stacked on #947 (#884). Fork synced at v0.18.0. Effort: medium.\n\nWhat changed: `list_features` no longer carries its own `outward()` winding helper; it calls `pick::align::outward_normal` (made `pub(crate)`), the helper WCS picks use, with the part's placement (`model::transform_of`) as the pose. Where `outward_normal` refuses (open/inside-out shell, no usable plane) the row keeps the canonical plane normal, placed by `world_dir`, so a listing never fails on one face (the old zero-winding fallback).\n\nPinned by: `mcp_pick::list_features_normal_follows_the_part_placement` (boss turned 90 deg about Y: caps read side, normals -X/+X; turned 180 deg: bottom cap up, top down); `list_features_facing_follows_the_outward_side` still green.\n\nTested: mcp_pick, mcp, mcp_setup, mcp_model, mcp_vise, mcp_plate, pick*, plane_align*, points_align, axis_align, wcs_align, winding_align, setup_align, feature_pick; clippy -D warnings camcraft-app. Not exercised: GUI; perf on very large meshes (outward_normal re-hashes the facets per face; winding verdict is memoized).\n\nChangelog: list_features reports each face's normal and facing via the shared outward-normal helper, where the part sits (#956, #947)\n\nFixes #956\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
